From 538aba8af0e56aa9d387dd5e9d488122f9d6f234 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Arkadiusz=20Mi=C5=9Bkiewicz?= <arekm@maven.pl>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 10:59:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix bug #80024: Duplication of info about inherited socket
 after pool removing

When a reload drops the socket count below a 128-socket set boundary,
the stale FPM_SOCKETS_<n> env var survives the re-exec and the next
reload imports the old sockets again (duplicated, leaked fds).

The test needs the tester.inc/logtool.inc reload helpers from the same
upstream commit (included).

Origin: upstream, https://github.com/php/php-src/commit/c483b59124bda89f86d8a54bcbdb8e5b89fa40ea
Bug: https://bugs.php.net/80024
---
